    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Lumen Technologies, Inc., also known as Lumen Technologies, is a public company headquartered in Monroe, Louisiana, with SEC CIK 0000018926 and ticker LUMN. Its website describes the company as providing a global fiber network, secure networking, edge cloud, and AI-ready infrastructure to connect people, data, and apps. The site positions Lumen as \"the enterprise-ready backbone of the AI economy,\" citing an expansive fiber footprint and reduced latency.\n\nThe company's site highlights customer examples: Arctic Glacier replaced manual operations with built-in automation, the New York Yankees use diverse 100G paths and automatic failover for real-time scalability, and American Family Care, an urgent care provider scaling across 26 states, received a private low-latency network for AI workloads. The site also says Prometheus Hyperscale anticipates cutting power consumption by 50% while keeping performance steady, and describes retail network security for transactions and DDoS protection with AI-driven personalization.\n\nLouisiana records list 57 legal matters associated with the company. No specific product names or lawsuits are listed in the available data.",
